From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WASM: stop formatting when EditEngine auto-splits an oversized paragraph

BUG-26. ImpEditEngine::ImpInsertText caps a paragraph at MAXCHARSINPARA
(0x3FFF - CHARPOSGROW = 16367; editeng/source/editeng/impedit.hxx:84) and pushes
the remainder into a NEW paragraph. That break is a text POSITION with no
counterpart in the source string, so the WASM insert-then-format loops -- which
advance a cursor by SOURCE lengths -- fall one position behind per split and
format every later run over the wrong characters.

Measured on a purpose-built fixture (a paragraph of N 'a' followed by a
10-character run styled 40pt bold red, PPTX -> ODP):

    17,000 chars (1 split):   <text:span T2>aZZMARKERZ</text:span>Z
    34,000 chars (2 splits):  <text:span T2>aaZZMARKER</text:span>ZZ

The styled window slides left by exactly the number of splits. No text is lost --
this is purely formatting landing on the wrong characters, which is why it had
never been noticed.

The split point cannot be predicted without reimplementing EditEngine's backward
word-break search (impedit2.cxx:2802-2858), which hunts up to 84 characters for a
non-alphanumeric break with special cases for hyphen-minus before a digit and for
NBSP/NNBSP/ZWNBSP. Duplicating that here would be upstream logic able to drift
silently.

So: format the runs provably BEFORE any possible split, then stop for the whole
text body -- the drift carries across paragraph boundaries, so continuing would
mis-format later paragraphs too. 16367-84 is the earliest position EditEngine
could choose. Everything already inserted stays; only character formatting is
skipped, and only from the first run that could straddle a split. SAL_WARN names
the paragraph length and the run index.

Applied to both loops (shape.cxx and table/tablecell.cxx), which have the same
defect.

--- a/oox/source/drawingml/shape.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/drawingml/shape.cxx
@@ -2464,6 +2464,11 @@
                         {
                             xCursor->gotoStart(false);
 
+                            // BUG-26: set when an oversized paragraph makes the
+                            // cursor arithmetic untrackable; see the comment at the
+                            // run loop. Formatting stops for the WHOLE text body,
+                            // because the drift carries across paragraph boundaries.
+                            bool bFormattingAbandoned = false;
                             for (size_t iPara = 0; iPara < rParagraphs.size(); ++iPara)
                             {
                                 const auto& paragraph = rParagraphs[iPara];
@@ -2647,10 +2652,74 @@
                                         "WASM: paragraph properties not applied");
                                 }
 
+                                // BUG-26 — EditEngine silently splits an oversized
+                                // paragraph, and this loop's cursor arithmetic cannot
+                                // survive it.
+                                //
+                                // ImpEditEngine::ImpInsertText caps a paragraph at
+                                // MAXCHARSINPARA (0x3FFF - CHARPOSGROW = 16367,
+                                // editeng/source/editeng/impedit.hxx:84) and pushes the
+                                // remainder into a NEW paragraph. That break is a text
+                                // POSITION with no counterpart in the source string, so
+                                // this pass — which advances by SOURCE lengths — falls
+                                // one position behind per split and formats every later
+                                // run over the wrong characters.
+                                //
+                                // Measured on a purpose-built fixture, converting a
+                                // paragraph of N 'a' followed by a 10-character run
+                                // styled 40pt bold red:
+                                //     17,000 chars (1 split): <span>aZZMARKERZ</span>Z
+                                //     34,000 chars (2 splits): <span>aaZZMARKER</span>ZZ
+                                // i.e. the styled window slides left by exactly the
+                                // number of splits. No text is lost — this is purely
+                                // formatting landing on the wrong characters, which is
+                                // why it had never been noticed.
+                                //
+                                // Predicting the split count is NOT viable: EditEngine
+                                // walks backward up to 84 characters hunting a
+                                // non-alphanumeric break, with special cases for
+                                // hyphen-minus before a digit and for NBSP/NNBSP/ZWNBSP
+                                // (impedit2.cxx:2802-2858). Reimplementing that here
+                                // would duplicate upstream logic that can drift silently.
+                                //
+                                // So: format the runs that are provably BEFORE any
+                                // possible split, then stop. Everything already inserted
+                                // stays; only character formatting is skipped, and only
+                                // from the first run that could straddle a split. That is
+                                // strictly better than both silent misattribution and
+                                // dropping formatting for the whole shape.
+                                //
+                                // 16367 - 84 is the earliest position EditEngine could
+                                // choose to break at, so a run ending at or before it
+                                // cannot be affected.
+                                const sal_Int32 nEditEngineParaLimit = 16367 - 84;
+                                sal_Int32 nParaSourceChars = 0;
+                                for (const auto& rRunLen : rRuns)
+                                    nParaSourceChars += rRunLen->getText().getLength();
+                                const bool bParaWillSplit = nParaSourceChars > 16367;
+                                sal_Int32 nRunOffset = 0;
+
                                 for (size_t iRun = 0; iRun < rRuns.size(); ++iRun)
                                 {
                                     const auto& run = rRuns[iRun];
 
+                                    if (bParaWillSplit)
+                                    {
+                                        nRunOffset += run->getText().getLength();
+                                        if (nRunOffset > nEditEngineParaLimit)
+                                        {
+                                            SAL_WARN("oox.drawingml",
+                                                "WASM: paragraph of " << nParaSourceChars
+                                                << " chars exceeds EditEngine's " << 16367
+                                                << "-char limit; it will be auto-split and the"
+                                                   " formatting cursor cannot track it. Character"
+                                                   " formatting skipped from run " << iRun
+                                                << " of this text body (BUG-26). Text is intact.");
+                                            bFormattingAbandoned = true;
+                                            break;
+                                        }
+                                    }
+
                                     const RunFieldKind eFieldKind
                                         = (iRun < aRunFieldKind[iPara].size())
                                               ? aRunFieldKind[iPara][iRun]
@@ -2953,6 +3022,12 @@
                                         }
                                     }
                                 }
+                                // Once abandoned, every later position is unknown —
+                                // including the paragraph break below, whose count is
+                                // exactly what the split changed. Stop entirely.
+                                if (bFormattingAbandoned)
+                                    break;
+
                                 // Skip the newline if not last paragraph
                                 if (iPara < rParagraphs.size() - 1)
                                     xCursor->goRight(1, false);
--- a/oox/source/drawingml/table/tablecell.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/drawingml/table/tablecell.cxx
@@ -723,6 +723,10 @@
             {
                 xCursor->gotoStart(false);
 
+                // BUG-26: see the run loop below. Drift from an EditEngine
+                // auto-split carries across paragraphs, so formatting stops for
+                // the whole cell once it can no longer be tracked.
+                bool bFormattingAbandoned = false;
                 for (size_t iPara = 0; iPara < rParagraphs.size(); ++iPara)
                 {
                     const auto& paragraph = rParagraphs[iPara];
@@ -887,10 +891,46 @@
                                              "WASM: cell paragraph properties not applied");
                     }
 
+                    // BUG-26 — EditEngine silently splits a paragraph longer than
+                    // MAXCHARSINPARA (16367, editeng impedit.hxx:84), pushing the
+                    // remainder into a NEW paragraph. That break is a text POSITION with
+                    // no counterpart in the source string, so this pass — which advances
+                    // by SOURCE lengths — falls one position behind per split and formats
+                    // every later run over the wrong characters. Measured: a 17,000-char
+                    // paragraph shifts the next run's styling left by 1, a 34,000-char one
+                    // by 2. No text is lost; only formatting lands wrongly.
+                    //
+                    // The split point cannot be predicted without reimplementing
+                    // EditEngine's backward word-break search (impedit2.cxx:2802-2858), so
+                    // instead: format the runs provably BEFORE any possible split, then
+                    // stop. 16367-84 is the earliest position it could break at.
+                    const sal_Int32 nEditEngineParaLimit = 16367 - 84;
+                    sal_Int32 nParaSourceChars = 0;
+                    for (const auto& rRunLen : rRuns)
+                        nParaSourceChars += rRunLen->getText().getLength();
+                    const bool bParaWillSplit = nParaSourceChars > 16367;
+                    sal_Int32 nRunOffset = 0;
+
                     for (size_t iRun = 0; iRun < rRuns.size(); ++iRun)
                     {
                         const auto& run = rRuns[iRun];
 
+                        if (bParaWillSplit)
+                        {
+                            nRunOffset += run->getText().getLength();
+                            if (nRunOffset > nEditEngineParaLimit)
+                            {
+                                SAL_WARN("oox.drawingml",
+                                    "WASM: table cell paragraph of " << nParaSourceChars
+                                    << " chars exceeds EditEngine's 16367-char limit; it will be"
+                                       " auto-split and the formatting cursor cannot track it."
+                                       " Character formatting skipped from run " << iRun
+                                    << " of this cell (BUG-26). Text is intact.");
+                                bFormattingAbandoned = true;
+                                break;
+                            }
+                        }
+
                         // Style, then the run's own, then endParaRPr where n#759180
                         // says it applies. Was default-constructed; see above.
                         TextCharacterProperties aRunProps(aEffectiveRunProps(iRun));
@@ -1054,6 +1094,11 @@
                             }
                         }
                     }
+                    // Once abandoned every later position is unknown, including the
+                    // paragraph break below. Stop entirely.
+                    if (bFormattingAbandoned)
+                        break;
+
                     // Skip the newline if not last paragraph
                     if (iPara < rParagraphs.size() - 1)
                         xCursor->goRight(1, false);
